                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the real need`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Diagnostic interviews are in. Halford’s HR brief asks for modules on <strong>finance, strategy and “communication”</strong> — but the sponsor and the line managers describe a different problem: newly promoted managers are <em>not making cross-functional decisions or holding accountability</em>. That is a <strong>behaviour gap, not a knowledge gap</strong>. Separate the stated need from the diagnosed business challenge, write the target outcome the way the board will judge it, and decide which requested content is genuinely required versus comfort. Design to the brief and you build a well-reviewed programme that fails the business.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Choose the format and allocate £480,000`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Format is a <strong>strategic trade-off</strong>, not a logistics call. Fully residential is the premium experience at <em>~£3,400/head</em> — but 220 managers would need £748,000 against your fixed <strong>£480,000</strong>. Blended (cohort digital + in-person intensives + workplace projects) runs <em>~£1,900/head</em> and balances cost, reach and behaviour change. Self-paced digital is cheapest at <em>~£950/head</em> but weakest on behaviour. Reconcile your three best faculty’s <strong>18 available days</strong> to demand, and allocate the envelope across design, delivery, faculty and (next round) measurement.`,
